        "a": "Funding rates are periodic payments between traders in perpetual futures markets. They're designed to keep the perpetual contract price close to the underlying spot price. When the perpetual trades above spot (bullish market), funding is positive and longs pay shorts. When it trades below spot (bearish market), funding is negative and shorts pay longs."
